# Repo-root environment. Two consumers, deliberately sharing one file:
#
#   - docker compose, when it creates the postgres container
#   - db/drizzle.config.ts, when the migrator connects to it
#
# A password set in only one of those places is the failure this file exists
# to prevent. The per-service .env files (discord-monitor/.env and friends)
# are separate — they configure the running processes, not the database.
#
# DB_PASSWORD is written into the container the first time it is created and
# lives in the postgres_data volume from then on. Changing it later has no
# effect until the volume is destroyed: `pnpm db:reset`.
DB_PASSWORD=defaultpassword123
